                <pb facs="0671" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/7639.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-25T16:00:00-04:00">July 25, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>669. Your no. 864 of July 22, 10 a.m. Our basic interest in the mercury at
                    Kunming is a preclusive one. It is important that it does not fall into Japanese
                    hands. If the Russians acquire these stocks, please suggest that they be
                    transported by northwest route at early date. Keep the Department informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
